#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.425pt, 719.76pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 90.96pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 114pt, "Mechanical intelligence (MI)")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(220.075pt, 110.4pt, "1–5")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(230.92pt, 114pt, "—the concept of designing intelligence within the mechanical ")
  #line-at(90pt, 125.52pt, "domain of materials and structures—has recently emerged as a direction to enable autonomous ")
  #line-at(90pt, 137.04pt, "engineering systems with high performance, efficiency, and resilience. Instead of outsourcing ")
  #line-at(90pt, 148.56pt, "entirely to electronics and computers, MI envisions materials that store, process, and perceive ")
  #line-at(90pt, 160.08pt, "information, and adapt to environmental inputs through their intrinsic mechanical responses, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 171.36pt, "thereby reducing latency and energy overheads while improving robustness in extreme conditions ")
  #line-at(90pt, 182.88pt, "and resistance to cyber threats. These unique features and advantages make MI particularly critical ")
  #line-at(90pt, 194.4pt, "for the realization of emerging complex engineering systems demanding advanced autonomy, such ")
  #line-at(90pt, 205.92pt, "as smart robotics, adaptive infrastructure, automated vehicles, and personal wearables. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.96pt, "The foundation of MI lies in mechanical information processing and learning")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.905pt, 225.36pt, "6–9")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(441.75pt, 228.96pt, ", which requires a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 240.48pt, "memory module to retain knowledge from environments, a computing module to process, interpret, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 252pt, "and perceive information, and a physical communication interface that bridges the stored memory ")
  #line-at(90pt, 263.52pt, "with computation. A widely adopted strategy emulates the digital computing paradigm by ")
  #line-at(90pt, 275.04pt, "abstracting mechanical bits from multistable structures for non-volatile memory storage and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.56pt, "implementing logic operations via carefully designed quasi-static state transitions and snap-through ")
  #line-at(90pt, 297.84pt, "interactions")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.138pt, 294.24pt, "10–19")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(159.213pt, 297.84pt, ". However, scaling such logic-based architectures to high-level computing tasks—")
  #line-at(90pt, 309.36pt, "especially cognitive learning and adaptation—requires sequential cascading of numerous basic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 320.88pt, "logic components via complex mechanical coupling, where information is transferred between ")
  #line-at(90pt, 332.4pt, "modules through slow quasi-static signal propagation, limiting both operational efficiency and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 343.92pt, "architectural scalability. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 366.96pt, "Learning naturally demands substantially greater computing power, requiring systems to store and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 378.48pt, "reason information, perceive features, and make decisions under uncertain environments. Inspired ")
  #line-at(90pt, 390pt, "by artificial or biological neural architectures, morphological computing or physical neural ")
  #line-at(90pt, 401.52pt, "networks—including mechanical")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(234.249pt, 397.92pt, "20–24")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(252.324pt, 401.52pt, " or wave-based neural networks")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(399.673pt, 397.92pt, "25–29")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.748pt, 401.52pt, " and physical reservoir ")
  #line-at(90pt, 413.04pt, "computing (PRC)")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(168.648pt, 409.44pt, "30–35")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(186.723pt, 413.04pt, "—has emerged to pursue learning using architected metamaterials. This ")
  #line-at(90pt, 424.56pt, "approach supports higher-level cognitive tasks, such as machine-learning regression and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.84pt, "classification tasks, through distributed physical transformations while avoiding explicit logic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 447.36pt, "cascades. Yet, these systems often depend either on sophisticated structural optimization for task-")
  #line-at(90pt, 458.88pt, "specific training, or on complex nonlinear and dynamic reservoirs requiring external digital ")
  #line-at(90pt, 470.4pt, "readouts. Critically, learned input-output mappings emerge from opaque black-box correlations ")
  #line-at(90pt, 481.92pt, "within disordered and intractable structural responses, undermining reliability in scenarios ")
  #line-at(90pt, 493.44pt, "demanding transparent reasoning and preventing the establishment of predictive and transferable ")
  #line-at(90pt, 504.96pt, "design rules—factors crucial for robustly deploying MI in real-world applications.")
  #line-at(448.57pt, 504.96pt, "What is missing, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 516.48pt, "therefore, is a unified, efficient, and physically transparent framework that seamlessly couples ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528pt, "memory with other elements of intelligence within the mechanical domain, in which stored ")
  #line-at(90pt, 539.52pt, "information natively drives computation and perception, enabling learning and decision-making ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.04pt, "through interpretable and predictable mechanisms. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 573.84pt, "The goal of our research is to advance the state of the art by bridging the abovementioned missing ")
  #line-at(90pt, 585.36pt, "gap via creating a fundamentally different and transformative framework of ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.534pt, 585.36pt, "in-memory phononic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 596.88pt, "learning")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.581pt, 596.88pt, ". This approach harness elastic wave propagation in architected phononic metastructures ")
  #line-at(90pt, 608.4pt, "as an efficient and mechanistically explicit interface that directly connects memory and the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 619.92pt, "information processing for learning. Phononic metastructures")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(358.643pt, 616.32pt, "36,37")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.909pt, 619.92pt, " are an ideal medium for this role; ")
  #line-at(90pt, 631.44pt, "through rich wave dispersion, interference, and resonance, they can perform complex analog ")
  #line-at(90pt, 642.96pt, "computations at the speed of sound while supporting parallelism across frequencies and modes")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(511.155pt, 639.36pt, "38–")
  #line-at(90pt, 650.88pt, "40")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(97.23pt, 654.48pt, ", where these features will be leveraged to interact with and perceive information stored in non-")
  #line-at(90pt, 666pt, "volatile mechanical memory.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 689.04pt, "To realize the new concept and evaluate our hypotheses, we develop an innovative multistable ")
  #line-at(90pt, 700.32pt, "phononic metastructure testbed that encodes complex spatial information from environmental ")
]

// arXiv source page 4
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 422pt), 100.5pt, 321.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.425pt, 719.76pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 90.96pt, "inputs—such as payload or deformation patterns—into reconfigurable, stable metastructure states ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.48pt, "as non-volatile mechanical memory (Figure 1A). Wave-based mechanical perception and cognitive ")
  #line-at(90pt, 114pt, "learning capabilities are then investigated and demonstrated through exemplar pattern-recognition ")
  #line-at(90pt, 125.52pt, "tasks, where structured elastic wave propagation is harnessed to perform in-situ classification of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 137.04pt, "these encoded memory patterns (Figure 1B). Specifically, the innovation of this testbed, detailed ")
  #line-at(90pt, 148.56pt, "in the Results section, is that it functionally separates memory state switching from wave ")
  #line-at(90pt, 160.08pt, "propagation while coupling them through controllable, state-dependent interactions. It enables the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 171.36pt, "testbed to concurrently achieve most effective wave transmission and state switching via different ")
  #line-at(90pt, 182.88pt, "materials in different layers. As a consequence, the metastructure memory directly and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 194.4pt, "deterministically programs the system's elastic wave-propagation landscape, transforming the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 205.92pt, "stored information into rich vibrational modes via the formulation of elastic waveguides. In-situ ")
  #line-at(90pt, 217.44pt, "perception occurs in the frequency domain by harnessing vibrational localization modes: under ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.96pt, "different harmonic excitations, the memory-defined geometry localizes wave energy into distinct, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 240.48pt, "frequency-selective local waveguides, for example, along specific edges or corners, which acts as ")
  #line-at(90pt, 252pt, "spatial phononic “filters” to extract key features of the stored information. We then establish a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 263.52pt, "phononic learning framework to classify encoded memory patterns from the perceived knowledge ")
  #line-at(90pt, 275.04pt, "by applying input excitation waveforms in the forms of linearly weighted harmonic signals (Figure ")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.56pt, "1B). Instead of optimizing the structural geometry, our training process optimizes these input ")
  #line-at(90pt, 297.84pt, "waveforms to selectively activate or suppress feature-modes associated with specific memory ")
  #line-at(90pt, 309.36pt, "pattern classes, thereby redistributing wave energy across the output channels. The classification ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(97.44pt, 595.44pt, "Figure 1. In-memory phononic learning framework. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324.48pt, 595.44pt, "(A) Memory encoding in a multistable phononic ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 605.76pt, "metastructure. The two symmetric stable states of each unit cell module are abstracted as mechanical bits ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 616.08pt, "‘0’ and ‘1’ and can be independently programmed to write spatial information as non-volatile mechanical ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 626.4pt, "memory. (B) In-memory phononic learning for pattern recognition. Trainable input waveforms (linearly ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 636.96pt, "weighted superpositions of harmonic tones) probe class-specific, frequency-selective vibrational ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 647.28pt, "localization modes. The classification decision is inferred directly from the output energy per input channel ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 657.6pt, "with the energy distribution across channels as a physical analog of class probabilities. (C) Conceptual ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 667.92pt, "equivalence to physical reservoir computing: treating the wave physics as a physical analog neural network.")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 678.24pt, "The metastructure’s frequency responses form a fixed, high-dimensional, and interpretable physical ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 688.56pt, "reservoir in which diverse localization modes perceive class-specific geometric features, and the trainable ")
  #line-at(97.44pt, 698.88pt, "input waves act as a linear readout layer, combining extracted features for classification outputs.   ")
]

// arXiv source page 5
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.425pt, 719.76pt, "5 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 90.96pt, "decision is then inferred directly from the output energy distribution across channels, representing ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.48pt, "a physical analog of prediction probabilities. In principle, this architecture is inspired by but very ")
  #line-at(90pt, 114pt, "different to that of PRC, by keeping learning and decision in the phononic domain without relying ")
  #line-at(90pt, 125.52pt, "on an external electronic readout layer. It creates a wave-physics-informed analog neural network, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 137.04pt, "where individual frequency responses serve as fixed feature-extraction layers operating in parallel ")
  #line-at(90pt, 148.56pt, "across frequencies (i.e., constituting a physical reservoir), while the superposition principle allows ")
  #line-at(90pt, 160.08pt, "the input waveforms to act as a trainable linear output layer to combine perceived features and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 171.36pt, "perform classification (Figure 1C). This framework completes the entire information-processing ")
  #line-at(90pt, 182.88pt, "chain—from memory encoding to perceptual feature extraction to learned decision—within a single, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 194.4pt, "fixed mechanical substrate. The process is efficient, inherently parallel, and physically ")
  #line-at(90pt, 205.92pt, "interpretable, as each step is governed by predictable and traceable memory-wave interactions in ")
  #line-at(90pt, 217.44pt, "a structured medium, avoiding the black-box nature of disordered morphological systems. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.96pt, "Furthermore, the framework naturally exhibits versatile computing power for multi-tasking, where ")
  #line-at(90pt, 240.48pt, "different tasks can be executed with the same structure by simply updating the input waveforms. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 252pt, "We experimentally and numerically validate this in-memory phononic learning framework by ")
  #line-at(90pt, 263.52pt, "achieving high-accuracy recognition across a series of 2D spatial pattern classification tasks. By ")
  #line-at(90pt, 275.04pt, "unifying memory, perception, and learning through a physically interpretable and transparent ")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.56pt, "mechanism, we elevate the ambition from \"materials that compute\" to the next level – achieving ")
  #line-at(90pt, 297.84pt, "“cognitive materials” that learn and understand through their inherent wave physics, providing a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 309.36pt, "foundation for deployable and robust mechanically intelligent matter that can interpret, reason, and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 320.88pt, "adapt to dynamic, unpredictable, and data-rich environments. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 343.92pt, "Results ")
  #line-at(90pt, 366.96pt, "Metastructure design for programmable non-volatile mechanical memory and wave physics")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.222pt, 366.96pt, ". ")
  #line-at(90pt, 378.48pt, "As illustrated in Figure 2A, a three-layer multistable phononic metastructure is built that functionally ")
  #line-at(90pt, 390pt, "separates memory encoding from wave propagation while coupling them through controllable, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 401.52pt, "state-dependent interactions. It comprises an inner phononic plate, sandwiched by two outer ")
  #line-at(90pt, 413.04pt, "multistable layers that provide non-volatile mechanical memory.")
  #line-at(392.715pt, 413.04pt, "The inner plate is a locally ")
  #line-at(90pt, 424.56pt, "resonant phononic metamaterial consisting of periodic square units, each containing a central ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.84pt, "resonator mass connected to a square frame through four thin beams (Figure 2B). This layer is ")
  #line-at(90pt, 447.36pt, "purposefully fabricated from a low-damping material to preserve high-fidelity wave responses as ")
  #line-at(90pt, 458.88pt, "needed for wave-based information processing. The top and bottom layers are arrays of curved-")
  #line-at(90pt, 470.4pt, "beam bistable elements mounted in a rigid frame, made from soft materials to facilitate effective ")
  #line-at(90pt, 481.92pt, "state-switching for mechanical memory encoding and storage. Each opposing bistable pair is ")
  #line-at(90pt, 493.44pt, "aligned with one inner-layer resonator so that the three pieces form a single cell multistable module ")
  #line-at(90pt, 504.96pt, "(Figure 2C), which functions as a mechanical memory bit that can be independently programmed ")
  #line-at(90pt, 516.48pt, "to write information. To physically link the stored memory to wave physics, permanent magnet disks ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528pt, "are affixed to the center of each outer bistable element and to each inner-layer resonator mass. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 539.52pt, "The magnets are axially magnetized and positioned to generate repulsive forces between the inner ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.04pt, "resonator and its two outer counterparts. State-switching of the bistable pair changes the inter-")
  #line-at(90pt, 562.32pt, "magnet distance and thus modulates the local coupling. Here, we consider the two symmetric ")
  #line-at(90pt, 573.84pt, "stable states for each module as mechanical bits ‘0’ and ‘1’, where bit ‘0’ means both outer bistable ")
  #line-at(90pt, 585.6pt, "elements are switched outward with an inter-magnet distance of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(392.112pt, 585.6pt, "𝑑")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(397.908pt, 587.76pt, "!")
