#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.425pt, 719.76pt, "8 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 90.96pt, "We then generalize the analysis to periodic supercells by considering different spatial memory bit ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.48pt, "distributions within 2-by-2-cell and 3-by-3-cell units, which leads to more diverse wave behaviors. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 114pt, "Accounting for periodicity and symmetry-induced equivalence, we identify 30 independent bit ")
  #line-at(90pt, 125.52pt, "configurations (Figure 3E). For each configuration, the corresponding bandgap frequency regions ")
  #line-at(90pt, 137.04pt, "are calculated, as summarized in Figure 3F, where the horizontal axis represents the indexes of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 148.56pt, "different memory configurations and the vertical columns show the corresponding bandgap ")
  #line-at(90pt, 160.08pt, "regions. We observe rich memory-dependent wave characteristics where each configuration ")
  #line-at(90pt, 171.36pt, "produces a unique band diagram. Even with identical percentages of ‘0’/‘1’ bit ratio but different ")
  #line-at(90pt, 182.88pt, "spatial distributions, the band diagrams can be entirely distinct, which can generate additional band ")
  #line-at(90pt, 194.4pt, "branches across different frequencies. Physically, different arrangements of mechanical bits modify ")
  #line-at(90pt, 205.92pt, "local resonances and couplings between units, which leads to lattice symmetry breaking and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 217.44pt, "branch degeneracies splitting in diverse ways (see Supporting Information, Section S5 for more ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.96pt, "details of supercell dispersion analysis). This establishes a predictable and deterministic mapping ")
  #line-at(90pt, 240.48pt, "between the encoded memory states and the resulting wave-propagation landscape. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 252pt, "Fundamentally, it converts the memory into rich phononic information carried by the wave ")
  #line-at(90pt, 263.52pt, "transmission spectrum that specifies the frequency channels conveying the stored information. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 286.56pt, "Frequency-selective wave energy localizations for memory-pattern feature perception. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(502pt, 286.56pt, "With ")
  #line-at(90pt, 297.84pt, "the fundamental wave physics uncovered, we now investigate to discover how these memory-")
  #line-at(90pt, 309.36pt, "programmed phononic properties enable a more sophisticated capability: frequency-selective wave ")
  #line-at(90pt, 320.88pt, "energy localization that performs feature-level perception of stored information. While previous ")
  #line-at(90pt, 332.4pt, "research has exploited rich waveguiding behavior in phononic metamaterials ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(450.585pt, 328.8pt, "36,41–44")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(477.695pt, 332.4pt, ", such as ")
  #line-at(90pt, 343.92pt, "defect-induced energy confinement along specific paths or topological-symmetry-breaking-induced ")
  #line-at(90pt, 355.44pt, "edge or corner modes, we uniquely utilize these phenomena to realize a mechanical perception ")
  #line-at(90pt, 366.96pt, "system where the wave energy localization modes selectively perceive and extract informative ")
  #line-at(90pt, 378.48pt, "geometric features of the stored memory patterns.")
  #line-at(90pt, 401.52pt, "Here, we exploit defect-induced wave energy localization, where the ‘defect’ comes from the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 413.04pt, "mechanical bit reconfiguration under information writing. We first uncover the fundamental principle ")
  #line-at(90pt, 424.56pt, "through dispersion analysis on a strip supercell containing a single programmed defect state. When ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.84pt, "a single unit within a uniform background is switched to a different memory bit, it creates a local ")
  #line-at(90pt, 447.36pt, "defect with resonance perturbation that traps wave energy locally at specific frequencies. For ")
  #line-at(90pt, 458.88pt, "instance, in a strip of uniform '0' bits, programming the central unit to '1' bit (referred to as Type I ")
  #line-at(90pt, 470.4pt, "encoding) introduces sharp defect modes within the original bandgap of the corresponding defect-")
  #line-at(90pt, 481.92pt, "free strip, as indicated by red dots in Figure 4A, left, concentrating vibrational energy precisely at ")
  #line-at(90pt, 493.44pt, "the defect unit. Conversely, in a strip of uniform '1' bits, programming the central unit to '0' (referred ")
  #line-at(90pt, 504.96pt, "to as Type II encoding) generates defect modes within the foundation-induced bandgap (Figure ")
  #line-at(90pt, 516.48pt, "4A, right), with similar spatial localization but at entirely different frequencies. The existence of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528pt, "these frequency-selective defect modes is further validated through full-scale metastructure ")
  #line-at(90pt, 539.52pt, "experiments and simulations, as shown in Figure 4B, where different-frequency waves can be ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.04pt, "selectively guided and localized along defected paths by reconfiguring the metastructure memory ")
  #line-at(90pt, 562.32pt, "states at excitation frequencies predicted by the eigen-frequency ranges of these defect-mode ")
  #line-at(90pt, 573.84pt, "bands. This frequency-selective localization provides a direct mechanism for processing the stored ")
  #line-at(90pt, 585.36pt, "information: defect modes act as spatial phononic filters, producing locally enhanced responses at ")
  #line-at(90pt, 596.88pt, "the programmed sites so that patterns encoded in the memory can be read from the scattering ")
  #line-at(90pt, 608.4pt, "wavefields. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 631.44pt, "This defect-mode physics scales elegantly to complex 2D patterns, enabling rich feature-level ")
  #line-at(90pt, 642.96pt, "perception. As illustrated in Figure 4C, when encoding complex spatial information, such as letters ")
  #line-at(90pt, 654.48pt, "‘")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(92.222pt, 654.48pt, "U")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.443pt, 654.48pt, "’ and ‘")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.103pt, 654.48pt, "M")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(133.433pt, 654.48pt, "’ into the metastructure memory, the system generates a set of distinct and diverse defect ")
  #line-at(90pt, 666pt, "modes that naturally decompose the patterns into constituent geometric features. Each defect ")
  #line-at(90pt, 677.52pt, "mode localizes wave energy at specific locations, such as edges, sharp corners, or junctions, with ")
  #line-at(90pt, 689.04pt, "the spatial wave energy distribution directly mapping to particular geometric characteristics of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 700.32pt, "encoded memory pattern.")
  #line-at(208.609pt, 700.32pt, "Crucially, these feature-modes resonate at distinct frequencies due to ")
