#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(510.85pt, 719.76pt, "11 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 90.96pt, "trainable input waveforms then act as a linear output layer, combining these perceived features to ")
  #line-at(90pt, 102.48pt, "perform classification. While standard PRC often relies on disordered systems to generate complex ")
  #line-at(90pt, 114pt, "nonlinear dynamics needed for a rich feature space, our system uses rich and predicable wave ")
  #line-at(90pt, 125.52pt, "physics from a structured metastructure medium. This ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(340.354pt, 125.52pt, "crucial difference")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.254pt, 125.52pt, " ensures that the high-")
  #line-at(90pt, 137.04pt, "dimensional feature mapping ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(227.524pt, 137.04pt, "emerges from physically traceable and interpretable localization ")
  #line-at(90pt, 148.56pt, "modes")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(120.015pt, 148.56pt, ", rather than from the opaque, black-box dynamics. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.22pt, 148.56pt, "More importantly, we realize learning ")
  #line-at(90pt, 160.08pt, "and decision entirely within the phononic domain, which eliminates the need for the digital or analog ")
  #line-at(90pt, 171.36pt, "electronic readout layers that are requisite in PRC, moving toward to truly self-contained cognitive ")
  #line-at(90pt, 182.88pt, "mechanical intelligence.")
  #line-at(90pt, 205.92pt, "Task 1: Geometric pattern classification")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(265.728pt, 205.92pt, ". To validate the in-memory phononic learning framework, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 217.44pt, "we first pursue a proof-of-concept task to classify geometric pattern shapes—squares, triangles, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.96pt, "and crosses—encoded into the metastructure memory. These patterns are randomly generated ")
  #line-at(90pt, 240.48pt, "with diverse scales and locations (Figure 5A and 5E). We evaluate both Type I (pattern as ‘1’s) and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 252pt, "Type II (pattern as ‘0’s) encoding schemes using a dataset of 150 samples (50 per class of pattern), ")
  #line-at(90pt, 263.52pt, "with 20% samples reserved for testing. The framework achieves 100% classification training and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 275.04pt, "testing accuracy for both encoding types in simulation, as indicated in Figure 5C and 5G, where ")
  #line-at(90pt, 286.56pt, "the output energy profiles from the well-trained input channels under each sample are plotted, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 297.84pt, "revealing that the highest energy outputs always come from the targeted channel. To gain more ")
  #line-at(90pt, 309.36pt, "physical insight, Figure 5B and 5F plot the frequency component weightings from the learned input ")
  #line-at(90pt, 320.88pt, "channels for each case, as well as the corresponding mean frequency response among each class ")
  #line-at(90pt, 332.4pt, "of patterns. It is noticed that, for each input channel, those most significant frequency components ")
  #line-at(90pt, 343.92pt, "with higher weightings concentrate on well-isolated resonance peaks for the targeted class while ")
  #line-at(90pt, 355.44pt, "being off resonance for the other two classes. It reveals a ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(370.345pt, 355.44pt, "physics-grounded strategy")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(489.821pt, 355.44pt, " of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 366.96pt, "proposed framework, where the training selects a sparse set of frequencies at which each input ")
  #line-at(90pt, 378.48pt, "wave only activates the corresponding class-specific localization modes while suppressing the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 390pt, "modes associated with the completing classes, and as a result, the output energy across channels ")
  #line-at(90pt, 401.52pt, "is redistributed with optimally enhanced vibration energy level at the corrected channel. This ")
  #line-at(90pt, 413.04pt, "observation is further confirmed by examining the output wavefields of the metastructure under the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 424.56pt, "well-trained input waves. For instance, Figure 5D and 5H visualize the scattering wavefields under ")
  #line-at(90pt, 436.08pt, "the three well-trained channels for selected samples. We observe that ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(404.729pt, 436.08pt, "𝐼")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(407.71pt, 438.24pt, "\"")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(412.175pt, 436.08pt, " activates square-related ")
  #line-at(90pt, 447.84pt, "modes with energy localization at the diagonal corners of squares, while ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.682pt, 447.84pt, "𝐼")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(433.885pt, 450pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(438.976pt, 447.84pt, " activates triangle-")
  #line-at(90pt, 459.6pt, "related modes along the triangle's inclined edges, and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(372.48pt, 459.6pt, "𝐼")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.684pt, 461.76pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.175pt, 459.6pt, " selects cross-related modes ")
  #line-at(90pt, 471.12pt, "concentrating energy at the intersection region. This demonstrates that the learning process ")
  #line-at(90pt, 482.64pt, "automatically identifies and leverages the most geometrically discriminative features for ")
  #line-at(90pt, 494.16pt, "classification. Experimental validation of the geometric pattern classification task is shown in Figure ")
  #line-at(90pt, 505.68pt, "6, using a set of 54 training and 18 testing samples under Type I encoding. Figure 6A presents the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 517.2pt, "measured steady-state wavefields for representative samples at six excitation frequencies that ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528.72pt, "selectively activate each class-related feature modes, revealing the perception capability of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 540pt, "testbed. Figure 6B plots the normalized output energies across the trained input channels for all ")
  #line-at(90pt, 551.52pt, "samples, where 53 out of 54 training samples and all testing samples are correctly recognized ")
  #line-at(90pt, 563.04pt, "despite experimental noise, validating the effectiveness of the proposed framework. (see ")
  #line-at(90pt, 574.56pt, "Supporting Information, Section S8 for more details of numerical and experimental validations of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 586.08pt, "geometric pattern classification tasks). ")
  #line-at(90pt, 609.12pt, "Furthermore, by comparing the results from Type I and Type II encoding schemes, we find that the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 620.64pt, "quality of wave localization directly impacts learning efficiency and confidence. Although both ")
  #line-at(90pt, 632.16pt, "achieve 100% accuracy, we quantify the confidence of the results by the average normalized ")
  #line-at(90pt, 643.68pt, "energy in the targeted channels across all samples, which is equal to the sample-averaged ")
  #line-at(90pt, 655.2pt, "predicted probability of the true class.  Type II encoding, which produces strong, well-separated ")
  #line-at(90pt, 666.48pt, "defect modes within a wide foundation-induced bandgap, requires only 8 frequency components ")
  #line-at(90pt, 678pt, "across all input channels and leads to a high confidence of 0.985, indicating that nearly all vibration ")
  #line-at(90pt, 689.52pt, "energy concentrates in the correct channels with minimal leakage to the untargeted ones. By ")
  #line-at(90pt, 701.04pt, "contrast, for Type I encoding, the defect modes appear in narrower local resonant bandgap ")
]

